From: TicWatch Nerves maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: rover: remove absent CPU cluster

SDM429 inherits the eight-core MSM8937 topology, but the watch only has
the four cores at MPIDR 0x100..0x103.  Linux attempts to start cpu@0..3,
PSCI rejects them with -EINVAL, and psci-cpuidle then unregisters idle
support for every CPU when it encounters those unusable nodes.

Remove the absent cluster for rover.  This leaves the four running cores
contiguous in Linux and permits PSCI idle state registration. In the 7.1
tree the absent nodes are labelled cpu0..cpu3 (cpu4..cpu7 in 6.15).

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm429w-mobvoi-rover.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm429w-mobvoi-rover.dts
@@ -8,6 +8,15 @@
 #include "sdm429w.dtsi"
 #include "pm660.dtsi"
 
+/delete-node/ &cpu0;
+/delete-node/ &cpu1;
+/delete-node/ &cpu2;
+/delete-node/ &cpu3;
+
+&{/cpus/cpu-map} {
+	/delete-node/ cluster0;
+};
+
 / {
 	interrupt-parent = <&intc>;
 	#address-cells = <2>;
